OL,3,AWater firm pleads guilty after four
OL,4,Akilled in blast
OL,5,
OL,6,FA water firm has pleaded guilty to
OL,7,Fhealth and safety charges after an
OL,8,Fexplosion at one of its sites killed
OL,9,Ffour workers, including a teenage
OL,10,Fapprentice.
OL,12,FLuke Wheaton, 16, Ray White, 57, Brian
OL,13,FVickery, 63, and Mike James, 64, died
OL,14,Fin the blast in a silo at Wessex
OL,15,FWater's treatment site in Avonmouth,
OL,16,FBristol, in December 2020.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
